== Trivia ==
* The Leper and Leper Flesh enemies were added in [[Booster Pack #5]].
* The Mulligan, Mulligoon, Hive, and {{e|Swarmer}} are all the same monster in stages of decay and infestation.
* In the original ''Binding of Isaac'', when a Mulligan self-detonated, the explosion would not break [[rock]]s.
* Mulligans will start running in random directions instead of directly away from Isaac if he stays close to them for long enough. This behavior also applies to {{e|Small Baby Long Legs}}.
* In the game's files, there is an unused Mulliboom self-detonation animation, an unused graphic of a Hive with a Mulligoon's face, and an unused graphic of the {{dlc|a}} Drowned Hive with a blue-tinted Mulligoon's face.
* {{dlc|a}} Drowned Hives, along with {{e|Drowned Charger}}s (name of Drowned Charger wasn't revealed), were revealed for ''Afterbirth'' in [https://web.archive.org/web/20190316152608/http://bindingofisaac.com/post/125792901269/double-vision-afterbirth-update-18 this official ''Binding of Isaac'' post].
* {{dlc|a+}} A leper is a person who suffers from [[wikipedia:Leprosy|leprosy]], which is a contagious disease that causes discoloration and lumping on the skin plus disfigurement and deformities.
* {{dlc|r}} Due to the Holy Mulligan leaving behind Embryos on death, it could be suggested that it transforms Embryos into the Small Angelic Babies it spawns.
* {{dlc|r}} Holy Mulligans, {{e|Holy Bony|text=Holy Bonies}}, and {{e|Holy Eye}}s originated as cards from the card game '''The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls'''.
* {{dlc|r}} Gas Dwarves used to be called Fartigans.
* {{dlc+|r}} [[Anti:Prey|Prey]], [[Anti:Mullighoul|Mullighouls]], and [[Anti:Bouncer|Bouncers]] originate from the ''Antibirth'' mod. In ''Antibirth'', Mullighouls could also appear in {{S|Mausoleum}} and had 13 stage hp.{{dlc-}}

